      "dom_id": "question-26412",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The point $Q$ with coordinates $(1,1)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(-x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The transformation $y=f(-x)$ reflects the curve $y=f(x)$ in the $y$-axis.\n\nFirst, notice that the point $P(1,1)$ lies $1$ unit to the *right* from the $y$-axis. So, under the action of the transformation, this point will be reflected $1$ unit to the *left* from the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253341/assets/e39b804eef0617e89d43808793c844f1223a427493e8b6554cc7ad25477f7ddc.png)\n\nWe conclude that the point $(-1,1)$ must lie on the graph of $y=f(-x).$",
